# Per-segment dispatch floor of split containers, whole YOLOv8 family, Phoenix NPU Device 0
UTC:      2026-09-20 17:14:47Z
MACHINE:  DESKTOP-CBL5NUA (Desktop 2, Ryzen 7 8700G, XDNA1 Phoenix)
ENV:      mlir-aie-iron (Python 3.13)
COMMIT:   ignite-xdna Canary 88c4605 (detached worktree split-audit)
COMMAND:  python tools/engine_dispatch_floor_split.py build/<c>.ignite --iters {300|200} --warmup {20|15}
IMAGE:    assets/bus.jpg    ITERS: 300 for n/pose/s/m, 200 for l/x (same for the NOP arm)
XRT-SMI:  'No hardware contexts running on device' checked before EVERY container and after the last

Method: the NOP copy sets every weight packet's op to NOP, so the cores still acquire every weight
packet, consume every activation packet and emit every output object; only the arithmetic is skipped.
Floor = NOP dispatch, compute = real minus NOP. Per-segment times are GraphSession.dispatch()'s own
last_segment_ms. These containers are --decouple-weights, so the NOP copy writes its own _nop.weights
sidecar and rewrites graph_engine.weights_sha256 to match. Task and byte counts come from
tools/shim_channel_audit.py over each container's own insts blobs.

